# Copyright (C) 2026 Antony Stubbs and contributors
#
# Read this together with the Java demo's Dockerfile
# (parallel-consumer-proxy-clients/parallel-consumer-proxy-client-java/demo/Dockerfile), which is
# the only build in this repository whose context is the repository rather than one module.
#
# That departure is safe only because of this file. The rule it bends - stated in the C++ client's
# Dockerfile - exists so a build never uploads other agents' target/ output, and concurrent
# worktrees under .claude make that a real cost rather than a theoretical one. IF YOU ADD A BUILD
# OUTPUT DIRECTORY TO THIS REPO, ADD IT HERE.
#
# The C++ and Swift client builds are unaffected: their context is their own module directory, and
# a build reads the .dockerignore of ITS OWN context root - so this file governs only the demo
# build. Neither of those modules carries one today, which is fine while their contexts stay small.

**/target/
**/build/
.git/
.claude/
.idea/
**/*.iml
**/*.log
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
